Date: Mon, 2 Nov 2026 19:54:10 +0700
Subject: [PATCH 4/7] Apply security policies to HTTP SQL and Arrow Flight SQL
 queries

The MySQL protocol marks every relation of a statement so the analyzer
applies column masking and row access policies to it. The FE's HTTP SQL API
(/api/v1/catalogs/<c>/databases/<d>/sql) and Arrow Flight SQL never marked
them, so a user under a mask or row filter read every row and column in the
clear through either.

Add SecurityPolicyRewriteRule.markRelationsForRewrite (named as in upstream
PR #78049, which fixes the same gap on main) and call it from the HTTP SQL
processor, the Flight SQL processor and the Flight prepared-statement schema
analysis.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
